From ea3b8c920e388be0964899f205cdf7dbc76135d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:06:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tank eject to a cauldron: a tank's output face fills an empty
 cauldron beside it with a bucket of water or lava

The one fluid handler vanilla blocks have (NeoForge's cauldron wrapper takes a whole bucket at once): a mod tank that gives through a face, holds a bucket or more of water or lava and moves at least that a tick fills the empty cauldron there. A single tank now drains too (the tank transfers used to need two block entities).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYe92n7spgy8vtm4CovRWA
